Edge case: if the value was also present under another key before removal, then after removal, that value may still be present. The spec says "value returned by the remove operation is not present in the map afterwards". This would be false if the value existed elsewhere. But maybe they assume values are unique? Not necessarily. But we follow spec.

Thus assert statement: `assert \old(this.containsKey(key)) => !this.containsValue(\result);`

